{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1","name":"The Sith Empire","source":{"id":"source:reference-303e4cc32aa1a8e1","title":"The Sith Empire","revision":24810,"timestamp":"2024-11-06T22:03:39Z","sha256":"11d69664e2a2ce137438933bb492153be328175c492e87f864f389394a58dc3f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24810","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Sith%20Empire&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-303e4cc32aa1a8e1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The reinvented Sith Empire of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Revan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Revan"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Malak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Malak","referenceId":"reference:9428775bff11dbd6"}," is a massive galaxy-threatening organization on par with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}," of the original ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars"]}," trilogy. This version of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," has it all, from huge battleships and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," to countless shocktroopers of both the \"normal\" and Force-using variety. They even have a Death Star-like superweapon, in the form of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Star Forge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Star_Forge"},". Technology and military engagements naturally play a major role for these Sith, since a show of overwhelming force is a prized strategy. Nonetheless, this revised Sith Empire has not abandoned its supernatural roots, training an army of acolytes in an academy on the ancient Sith homeworld ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At the height of its power, The Sith Empire is much like ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}," in that it is highly organized and has the ability to wage an effective war against its enemies. Despite the inherently traitorous nature of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},", The Sith Empire's hierarchy is surprisingly rigid, and has a rank structure that ensures that all war efforts do not suffer from infighting.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At the top of the command structure are the two most prominent Sith Lords, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Revan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Revan"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Malak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Malak","referenceId":"reference:9428775bff11dbd6"}," (though Malak assumes sole control of The Sith Empire after betraying his master). A number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," serve under the two most prominent masters, including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Bandon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Bandon","referenceId":"reference:7833fd2616f2400c"},". Each being that achieves the full title of Dark Lord of the Sith is given control over some military or civilian assets; many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," are placed in charge of entire fleets or battalions, while others serve as the rulers of captured worlds. In many respects, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," are above and beyond the normal rank structure, and they have the final authority over admirals, commanders, and entire sector governments. In many ways, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," are comparable to the Moffs of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Sith Navy consists of all of the military ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," under the control of The Sith Empire. The Sith Navy is further subdivided into fleets, some of which are large enough to patrol an entire sector effectively. Each fleet is under the control of an admiral, like ",{"tag":"a","children":["Saul Karath"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Saul_Karath","referenceId":"reference:71c4ad7788fc4d79"},", though these admirals in turn answer to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"},". Fleets are further subdivided into battle groups, which usually consist of five to ten ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and various support craft. The descending order of ranks among the Sith Navy are admiral, vice admiral, commodore, captain, major, and lieutenant. All nonofficer personnel aboard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," in the Sith Navy are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Troopers"}," or specially assigned crewmembers, such as students from the Sith Academy on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"}," joining a crew for a special assignment.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though there is no formal Sith Army, the ground forces of The Sith Empire are an entity all on their own. Used not only in ground warfare but also in the occupation, policing, and pacification of captured worlds, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Troopers"}," and their officers fall directly under the command of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," they serve. While aboard ships of the Sith Navy they are under the command of the captain of the ship they serve on, but once planetside they report either to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"}," ruling that planet or to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"}," in command of the military efforts in the region. The highest-ranking Sith officers are commanders, who outrank colonels and lieutenants.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Among the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Troopers"},", there are truly only two designations: troopers and commandos, though neither truly outranks the other. Lieutenants and colonels in command of squads handle the front-line efforts of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Trooper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Trooper","referenceId":"reference:6f9f12c707e475f8"}," squads, reporting up the chain of command to colonels who apprise ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lords"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lords"}," of ongoing situations and ensure the Sith Lords' commands are carried out.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sith Empire Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sentinel Droid Mark I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sentinel_Droid_Mark_I","referenceId":"reference:5f8d64b952d59856"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Trooper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Trooper","referenceId":"reference:6f9f12c707e475f8"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Municipal Patrol Droid Mark I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Municipal_Patrol_Droid_Mark_I","referenceId":"reference:4b09fb8a8579e82b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Commando"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Commando","referenceId":"reference:d1c5b82a30c811e3"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href